=== src/main/resources/officefloor/README.md
# OfficeFloor REST wiring

Domain REST endpoints are declared here as OfficeFloor YAML, served by the
`officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` inside the Spring Boot host. Put them under `rest/api/` so
their paths start with `/api/` — `SpaConfig` only lets `/api/*` reach the backend; a non-`/api/`
path returns the SPA's `index.html` instead of your endpoint. Directory nesting maps to path
segments, so `rest/api/owners.GET.yml` → `GET /api/owners`. Each route is its own file:

```
# officefloor/rest/api/<path>.GET.yml   (or .POST.yml, {param}.GET.yml, ...)
service:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.<SomeLogic>   # a class with a service(...) method
```

The logic class's `service(...)` method takes injected dependencies (Spring `@Service` beans, the
data layer) and a `net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse<T>` to send the response.

(The `/actuator/health` readiness endpoint is Spring-side — Actuator — not an OfficeFloor route.)
=== src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__sheet.sql
-- A sheet: everything else in the app is kept per sheet. A row is created the first time its id
-- is loaded, so a sheet that was never loaded before starts empty.
CREATE TABLE sheet (
    id         VARCHAR(200) PRIMARY KEY,
    created_at TIMESTAMP    NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
=== src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/sheets/{sheetId}.PUT.yml
# Load a sheet by id: an id never used before starts an empty sheet.
validate:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet.ValidateSheetId
  next: ensure
ensure:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet.EnsureSheet
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond
respond:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet.RespondWithSheet
  govern: [ transaction ]
=== src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/signin.POST.yml
# Sign in by name (no password): the trimmed name is the user every later change is recorded by.
validate:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.session.ValidateSignIn
  next: respond
respond:
  class: net.officefloor.hq.app.session.RespondWithUser
=== src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/sheet/EnsureSheet.java
package net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;

public class EnsureSheet {
    public void ensure(@Val SheetResponse sheet, SheetRepository repository) {
        repository.ensure(sheet.id());
    }
}
=== src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/sheet/RespondWithSheet.java
package net.officefloor.hq.app.sheet;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Val;
import net.officefloor.web.ObjectResponse;

public class RespondWithSheet {
    public void respond(@Val SheetResponse sheet, ObjectResponse<SheetResponse> response) {
        response.send(sheet);
    }
}
